            NOT greedy, and not by choice. This API rejects temperature=0 outright ('does not support 0 with this model. Only the default (1) value is supported'), so the greedy discipline every local arm in this repo uses is unavailable. Both arms therefore run at the API's fixed default, which puts them on the WIDE noise floor this project measured for non-greedy runs -- 4 to 8 tasks per repeat, not the +/-1 of a greedy arm. Any delta smaller than about 8 tasks is not separable from noise here. The pair is still single-variable in the thing being tested: both arms are identical except reasoning_effort.
